{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-14 08:16:55 UTC] [Agent: Scribe Coder] [Project: council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration] FOUND IT! The test_session fixture uses @pytest.fixture instead of @pytest_asyncio.fixture. This causes pytest to treat it as a sync fixture that returns an async generator object instead of awaiting it and yielding the session_id. | file=tests/test_phase2_reconsolidation.py; fix=change @pytest.fixture to @pytest_asyncio.fixture; line=50; reasoning={\"how\": \"Change line 50 from @pytest.fixture to @pytest_asyncio.fixture, import pytest_asyncio at top of file\", \"what\": \"Fixture decorator mismatch: @pytest.fixture for async function means it returns the generator object directly, not the yielded value. Need @pytest_asyncio.fixture to properly handle async fixtures.\", \"why\": \"Tests receive async generator instead of session_id because pytest doesn't await the fixture\"}; root_cause=wrong_fixture_decorator; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T08:16:55.792178+00:00_f02302f5", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T08:16:55.792208+00:00"}
