{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-14 08:22:42 UTC] [Agent: Scribe Coder] [Project: council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration] Found implementation bug: _apply_reconsolidation calls apply_access_boost with wrong signature. Expected: (record: MemoryRecord, config, now). Actual: (current_strength, metadata, config). Need to fetch full MemoryRecord and pass it correctly. | correct_signature=(record: MemoryRecord, config, now=None); file=council_mcp/tools/ask_base.py; lines=921-925; reasoning={\"how\": \"Fetch MemoryRecord from database using fetch_persona_memory, pass to apply_access_boost, extract new strength from returned record\", \"what\": \"Code extracts strength and metadata from dict but AgentKit expects full MemoryRecord object. apply_access_boost returns tuple (MemoryRecord, bool).\", \"why\": \"API mismatch causing all reconsolidation attempts to fail silently\"}; wrong_call=(current_strength, metadata, config); priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T08:22:42.829136+00:00_bd9351ac", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T08:22:42.829168+00:00"}
