{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-14 08:26:05 UTC] [Agent: Scribe Coder] [Project: council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration] Fixed test expectation: AgentKit uses ADDITIVE boost (strength + 0.05), not MULTIPLICATIVE (strength * 1.05). Updated test to expect initial_strength + config.access_boost with 1.0 cap. | file=tests/test_phase2_reconsolidation.py; fix=additive boost calculation; new=min(1.0, initial_strength + config.access_boost); old=initial_strength * (1 + config.access_boost); reasoning={\"how\": \"Updated expected_strength formula and print statement to reflect actual boost behavior\", \"what\": \"Changed from percentage-based calculation to absolute addition with 1.0 capping\", \"why\": \"AgentKit's actual behavior is additive, not multiplicative\"}; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T08:26:05.464104+00:00_459d04ed", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T08:26:05.464138+00:00"}
