{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-14 08:28:34 UTC] [Agent: Scribe Coder] [Project: council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration] SUCCESS! All 6/6 Phase 2 reconsolidation tests PASSED. Test fixes complete: (1) Fixed async fixture decorators (pytest_asyncio.fixture), (2) Corrected store_memory return key (memory_id not id), (3) Fixed _apply_reconsolidation API usage (fetch MemoryRecord, call apply_access_boost correctly), (4) Updated metadata test for nested decay_history structure, (5) Fixed boost calculation expectation (additive not multiplicative). | fixes_applied=[\"async fixture decorators\", \"store_memory return key\", \"apply_access_boost API usage\", \"metadata structure expectations\", \"boost calculation formula\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Systematically debugged each failure, verified actual behavior against expectations, applied targeted fixes to both test file and implementation\", \"what\": \"Fixed 5 distinct issues: (1) pytest_asyncio fixture decorators for async fixtures, (2) result['memory_id'] not result['id'], (3) apply_access_boost(record, config, now) not (current_strength, metadata, config), (4) metadata['decay_history']['last_accessed'] not metadata['last_accessed'], (5) additive +0.05 boost not multiplicative *1.05\", \"why\": \"Tests failed due to fixture handling, API mismatches, and incorrect expectations\"}; test_file=tests/test_phase2_reconsolidation.py; tests_passing=6/6; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/council_agentkit_memory_decay_integration/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-14T08:28:34.388892+00:00_989a511e", "timestamp": "2026-01-14T08:28:34.388972+00:00"}
